CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ function type is a function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ multi-arg function type is a function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ object type is not a function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.fct]/7: cv-qualifiers added on top of a function type are ignored
(there are no cv-qualified function types).  A const-qualified template
parameter substituted with a function type must drop the const, so
is_const<const T> is false and the libstdc++ is_function<T> idiom
(!is_const<const T>) is true for function types.  Underlies std::decay's
function-to-pointer decay and constructing std::function from a function.
